course: dictionary
lesson: 10673
title: Unmown
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word unmown is built from two parts. The prefix un- means not, and mown means cut with a mower. So unmown means not cut by a mower, and a mower is the machine that cuts grass.
explain: Check the context. «Longer, unmown grass lets clover, daisies and other flowers bloom and feed bees and butterflies.» The word longer is a clue: grass that is not cut grows long. Try your meaning in the sentence: "long grass that has not been cut" makes sense, so you have understood it.
explain: Writers use unmown to paint a picture. «An unmown lawn» can suggest that nobody has looked after a garden for a while. The words around a word always give clues about its meaning and what it suggests.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unmown means not mown.
fact: «Unmown» means not cut by a mower.
fact: «Mown» is the past form of mow, which means to cut grass.
fact: Unmown grass is left to grow long, and it lets wildflowers, bees and butterflies thrive.
fact: «No Mow May» is a UK idea that asks people to skip mowing for a month.
exercise: «Longer, unmown grass lets clover and daisies bloom.» What does unmown mean? | *Not cut by a mower | Very wet from rain | Cut short by a mower | Painted green
exercise: The prefix un- is at the start of unmown. What does un- mean? | Under | Very big | *Not | Again
exercise: In «leave a patch unmown», what should you do to the patch? | Paint it blue | Dig it up | *Let it grow long | Cut it very short
test: «No Mow May» asks people to skip mowing for a month, so the grass can grow. What does skip mowing mean? | Buy a new mower | Water the grass every day | *Do not cut the grass | Cut the grass twice
test: Why might a science class study an unmown patch of lawn? | To make the lawn perfectly flat | To learn to ride a mower | To count the spiders in a barn | *To see how wildflowers, bees and butterflies live there
exam: Which sentence uses unmown correctly? | The mower unmown the lawn every day | Unmown means a very fast mower | *The meadow stayed unmown all summer, so wildflowers grew tall | Unmown is a kind of bird
